<title>UK: Merrill declines comment on UK job cuts.</title>
<headline>Merrill declines comment on UK job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Securities firm Merrill Lynch and Co on Tuesday declined to comment on market rumours that it was about to make substantial cuts to its UK equities market-making staff.</p>
<p>&quot;Merrill Lynch remains totally committed to retaining its leadership position in UK equities trading. It is not Merrill Lynch's policy to comment on market rumours,&quot; a spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Recent rumours have put the extent of possible job cuts at Merrill at up to 50 percent of its approximately 60 market making positions.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
